   "source": [
    "from langchain_google_genai import GoogleGenerativeAIEmbeddings\n",
    "from langchain_community.document_loaders import PyPDFLoader\n",
    "from langchain_text_splitters import RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter\n",
    "\n",
    "from pinecone import Pinecone, ServerlessSpec\n",
    "from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\n",
    "\n",
    "import google.generativeai as genai\n",
    "import re"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "d952ce35-0f57-4a47-8641-4e8036297557",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "GOOGLE_API_KEY= \"wgijnegaqeijfnwsfoawfnafoa"\n",
    "PINECONE_API_KEY= \"ewlkgnegleangalegnaegaedngaegnag"\n",
    "INDEX_NAME=\"ai-legal\"\n",
    "\n",
    "PDF_PATH= r\"C:\\Users\\test\\Desktop\\Projects\\Siena College\\Basic-Non-Disclosure-Agreement.pdf\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "56286f9b-df10-4354-964e-d9694d5a8c0e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# connect Pinecone\n",
    "# This connects Python app to Pinecone, which is used to store and search vector embeddings (numerical representations of text).\n",
    "\n",
    "pc = Pinecone(api_key=PINECONE_API_KEY)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "c4dddb23-e8b7-471b-a4e3-c497509e470b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Index ready!\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# create index if not exists (An index is like a database table for storing vectors.)\n",
    "\n",
    "if INDEX_NAME not in pc.list_indexes().names():\n",
    "    pc.create_index(\n",
    "        name=INDEX_NAME,\n",
    "        dimension=384,                      # all-MiniLM-L6-v2 dimension size\n",
    "        metric=\"cosine\",\n",
    "        spec=ServerlessSpec(\n",
    "            cloud=\"aws\",\n",
    "            region=\"us-east-1\"\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "index = pc.Index(INDEX_NAME)\n",
    "print(\"Index ready!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f397d941-33d5-44ec-ae45-d8978dd62abd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "| Parameter            | Meaning                                                                            |\r\n",
    "| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\r\n",
    "| `name`               | Name of your vector database                                                       |\r\n",
    "| `dimension=384`      | Size of the embedding vector (because `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` produces 384-dim vectors) |\r\n",
    "| `metric=\"cosine\"`    | How similarity is measured                                                         |\r\n",
    "| `cloud=\"aws\"`        | Hosting provider                                                                   |\r\n",
    "| `region=\"us-east-1\"` | Server location                                                                    |\r\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "46d70927-e76c-4f28-95c0-cc317c7b897d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "PDF pages: 2\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ====== LOAD PDF ======\n",
    "\n",
    "loader = PyPDFLoader(PDF_PATH)\n",
    "docs = loader.load()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"PDF pages:\", len(docs))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a90d9391-10da-492e-b5a6-f0a6af3c6883",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This uses LangChain’s PDF loader to read your PDF.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each page becomes a Document object with:\n",
    "* page_content → text\n",
    "* metadata → page number, file info"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "e41dacff-60fc-4288-b7be-d12e93f35c01",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Total Chunks: 8\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ====== SPLIT PDF TO CHUNKS(small pieces of text taken from a large document) ======\n",
    "\n",
    "splitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(\n",
    "    chunk_size = 1000,\n",
    "    chunk_overlap = 200\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "chunks = splitter.split_documents(docs)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Total Chunks:\", len(chunks))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d5c0a963-e30a-434a-b4fa-10cbc254b625",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "LLMs and embeddings work better with small text chunks instead of whole pages.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Setting             | Meaning                               |\r\n",
    "| ------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\r\n",
    "| `chunk_size=1000`   | Each chunk has ~1000 characters       |\r\n",
    "| `chunk_overlap=200` | 200 characters overlap between chunks\n",
    "This helps preserve context between chunks.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each PDF page is broken into multiple text chunks. These chunks will later be:\n",
    "* Converted into embeddings\n",
    "* Stored in Pinecone\n",
    "* Used for question answering / RAG |\r\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "fd650cff-4b80-49af-a232-041ace359e02",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ====== LOAD LOCAL EMBEDDING MODEL ======\n",
    "# (Free, no internet)\n",
    "\n",
    "model = SentenceTransformer(\"all-MiniLM-L6-v2\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e301ee5e-68c8-4f3f-8ab3-848cb14aba6a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This loads a local AI model that converts text into numbers (vectors).\n",
    "\n",
    "Important points:\n",
    "* Works offline (no internet)\n",
    "* Converts text → 384-dimensional vectors\n",
    "* Used for semantic search (meaning-based search)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "f4300b1b-084e-408e-95d1-7c195356b9bd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Upload complete!\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ====== EMBED + STORE IN PINECONE ======\n",
    "\n",
    "vectors = []  # this will hold (ID, embedding_vector, metadata)\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, ch in enumerate(chunks):\n",
    "\n",
    "    text = ch.page_content\n",
    "\n",
    "    vec = model.encode(text).tolist()   # Text → Numbers → Vector\n",
    "\n",
    "    vectors.append(\n",
    "        (str(i), vec, {\"text\": text})\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "# upload to pinecone (This sends all vectors to Pinecone.)\n",
    "index.upsert(vectors)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Upload complete!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "f77ef1b9-e754-4c73-a03d-46b75af3b26d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ================== INIT ==================\n",
    "genai.configure(api_key=GOOGLE_API_KEY)   # This connects the app to Google’s Gemini AI model so it can generate answers.\n",
    "\n",
    "pc = Pinecone(api_key=PINECONE_API_KEY)\n",
    "index = pc.Index(INDEX_NAME)\n",
    "\n",
    "embed_model = SentenceTransformer(\n",
    "    \"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "llm = genai.GenerativeModel(\n",
    "    model_name=\"models/gemini-2.5-flash\"\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4afab70f-82a2-4935-b4d2-54b12f31fd9c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Gemini LLM Model**\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the AI brain that:\n",
    "* Reads retrieved context\n",
    "* Understands the question\n",
    "* Generates the final answer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "445d44d1-c5b3-42bf-85ed-ef324e2ca2e5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ================== HELPERS ==================\n",
    "def is_greeting(text):\n",
    "    greetings = r\"\\b(hi|hello|hey|good morning|good afternoon|good evening)\\b\"\n",
    "    return re.search(greetings, text.lower()) is not None"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a95e2f0b-bf5e-4ddc-a1e7-8ef8617631cd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Detects if the user says:\n",
    "\n",
    "Hi, Hello, Good morning, Hey - So your chatbot can respond politely instead of searching the PDF."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "1d09ad30-6ee9-4a1a-8bf9-bab12c774ec1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ================== HELPERS ==================\n",
    "\n",
    "def retrieve_context(question, top_k=3):\n",
    "    query_vec = embed_model.encode(question).tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "    results = index.query(\n",
    "        vector=query_vec,\n",
    "        top_k=top_k,\n",
    "        include_metadata=True\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    contexts = []\n",
    "    for match in results[\"matches\"]:\n",
    "        contexts.append(match[\"metadata\"][\"text\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "    return \"\\n\\n\".join(contexts)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3f1b6fa5-b218-4c0a-b278-e3a2c2039c84",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "* This function finds relevant PDF content for a user’s question.\n",
    "* User’s question → numerical vector\n",
    "* Pinecone finds the top 3 most similar chunks from your PDF.\n",
    "* Each match contains the original chunk text.\n",
    "* Returns a single text block with all relevant PDF info."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "0d041e8a-4bea-4b77-9c2f-a1f11ed6c4c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ================== RAG RESPONSE ==================\n",
    "def rag_chat(question):\n",
    "    # Greeting handling\n",
    "    if is_greeting(question):\n",
    "        return \"👋 Hello! I’m your Legal Assistant. How can I help you today?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    context = retrieve_context(question)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Prompt\n",
    "    prompt = f\"\"\"\n",
    "You are a friendly and knowledgeable AI Legal assistant.\n",
    "\n",
    "Rules:\n",
    "- If context is relevant, answer ONLY from context\n",
    "- If context is weak or empty, answer generally but politely\n",
    "- Keep responses simple, clear, and conversational\n",
    "- Do NOT mention the word \"context\" in your answer\n",
    "\n",
    "Legal Content:\n",
    "{context}\n",
    "\n",
    "User Question:\n",
    "{question}\n",
    "\n",
    "Answer:\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    response = llm.generate_content(prompt)\n",
    "    return response.text.strip()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ad459a58-599e-419f-b282-6feca28b216c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**What is rag_chat()?**\n",
    "\n",
    "It is a function that:\n",
    "* Accepts a user question\n",
    "* Finds relevant PDF content (RAG)\n",
    "* Sends everything to Gemini AI\n",
    "* Returns a natural language answer\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why This is Called RAG?**\n",
    "\n",
    "RAG = Retrieval Augmented Generation\n",
    "\n",
    "Because:\n",
    "* Retrieval → Pinecone finds content\n",
    "* Generation → Gemini writes the answer\n",
    "* So your chatbot doesn’t hallucinate — it uses real PDF data.eturned\r\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "72381d53-c880-4f91-aa8a-7236cf06743c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "User Question\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Greeting? → Reply politely\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Find PDF content (Pinecone)\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Send to Gemini\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Answer returned"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "59c99c09-a480-4515-814c-a45f32680b70",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ================== CHAT LOOP ==================\n",
    "def chat_bot():\n",
    "    print(\"🤖 Course Assistant is running!\")\n",
    "    print(\"Ask anything about the Legal Document. Type 'exit' to quit.\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    while True:\n",
    "        user_input = input(\"You: \").strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "        if user_input.lower() in [\"exit\", \"quit\"]:\n",
    "            print(\"👋 Goodbye!\")\n",
    "            break\n",
    "\n",
    "        answer = rag_chat(user_input)\n",
    "        print(f\"Assistant: {answer}\\n\")"
   ]
  },
